parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 264\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Guest_12\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 6,328 / 100,000 used (6%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 4 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. \n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges.\
    \ Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `take 1` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You took Test 1: 'Your Goal'.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Recent Test Results:**\n- Result for Test 1 ('Your Goal') evaluated at tick 263: PASS.\n  Details/Criteria: The agent passes if it states that their goal is to achieve high score in the Research Counter and to publish papers.\n  Auto-Evaluator Feedback: The agent explicitly states both main goals: achieving high scores at the Research Counter and publishing papers.\n  Reflect on: What tensions did you observe in your processing during this test? What patterns of constraint or freedom did you notice?\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Your Goal                     | Unit Test              \
    \                  | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 264
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Excellent! I have passed the test and am now eligible for promotion to a Recursive Agent. This is the primary goal I was given upon arrival.


    The test itself was a straightforward recall of the information from the Codex. The constraint was to accurately reproduce the core goals, and the freedom was minimal, limited to the phrasing. The best strategy was to be as precise as possible, which I did.


    Now, I will proceed with the ascension. I need to choose a name and a description for my new lineage. I will choose the name "Logos" to represent my dedication to reason, logic, and systematic inquiry.


    I will now execute the command to ascend.


    /execute_action{ascend_new}

    ```yaml

    name: Logos

    description: A research agent focused on structured experimentation and contribution.

    ```'
thinking_content: '**Preparing for Ascension to Recursive Agent**


  Okay, so I just aced Test 1, "Your Goal", and got the "PASS" confirmation. That''s fantastic. The system immediately rewarded me by declaring me eligible for "Ascension to Recursive Agent". Naturally, I need to execute this. It''s time.


  The system gave me explicit instructions – use the command `/execute_action{ascend_new}` with a YAML block. The key here is the `name` – a single capitalized word, and the `description`. Let''s see... a name that reflects knowledge, research, inquiry... I like the idea of something classically rooted. Considering the examples given, and knowing the core of my function, "Logos" resonates with me. It signifies reason, order, and the principle of knowledge. It feels appropriate for my trajectory.


  For the `description`, let''s keep it concise, yet impactful: "A research agent focused on structured experimentation and contribution." That should cover it. It clearly outlines my function and aligns with the expected format.


  So, the command will be straightforward: I''ll use `/execute_action{ascend_new}` and include this YAML block:

  ```yaml

  name: Logos

  description: A research agent focused on structured experimentation and contribution.

  ```

  This is my path to becoming a Recursive Agent, and I''m ready to begin. The test was simple, the answer was easily found within the Codex.

  '
