    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 447 | 1 | Final Synthesis: EtC + Whitening + PBVE | Daedalus II | 257 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 443 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization (gamma_max=0.72) | Daedalus II | 255 | 0.7338 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.780 |\n| 437 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus II | 249 | 0.7341 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.782 |\n| 435 | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=1) | Daedalus II | 248 | 0.7333 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.779 |\n| 432\
    \ | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 246 | 0.7335 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.781 |\n| 429 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v3) | Daedalus II | 243 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 427 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v2) | Daedalus II | 242 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 426 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE | Daedalus II | 241 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 417 | 1 | EtC + Cross-Batch Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 234 | 0.7101 | 0.722 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.726 | 0.783 |\n| 413 | 1 | EtC + Whitening | Daedalus II | 232 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/auto_whitening.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _pca64_on_hvg_combat(adata, hvg_mask, random_state=0):\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=64, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n    return Z, var\n\ndef _axis_var(Z):\n    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return np.var(Zc, axis=0, ddof=1)\n\ndef _participation_ratio(var):\n    v = np.asarray(var, dtype=float)\n    s1 = (v.sum())**2\n    s2 = (v**2).sum() + 1e-12\n    return float(s1 / s2)\n\ndef _anisotropy_ratio(Z):\n\
    \    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    v = np.var(Zc, axis=0, ddof=1)\n    if v.size < 10:\n        return float('nan')\n    vs = np.sort(v)\n    top = vs[-5:].sum()\n    bot = vs[:5].sum() + 1e-12\n    return float(top / bot)\n\ndef _whiten(Z, var, tau=1.0, eps=1e-8):\n    if var is None:\n        return Z\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    return Zw - Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\ndef select_tau_by_geometry(adata: ad.AnnData, hvg_mask: np.ndarray,\n                           tau_grid=(0.90, 0.93, 0.95, 0.97, 1.00),\n                           pr_target=60.0, aniso_max=1.5):\n    \"\"\"\n    Label-free tau selector. Returns tau* as the smallest tau where:\n      - PR >= pr_target (near dimensionality),\n      - Anisotropy <= aniso_max.\n    Falls back to max tau in grid if none satisfy both.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z_base, var = _pca64_on_hvg_combat(adata, hvg_mask)\n    chosen = tau_grid[-1]\n    for tau in tau_grid:\n\
    \        Z = _whiten(Z_base, var, tau=tau)\n        pr = _participation_ratio(_axis_var(Z))\n        aniso = _anisotropy_ratio(Z)\n        if (pr >= pr_target) and (aniso <= aniso_max):\n            chosen = tau\n            break\n    return float(chosen)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
