    \ Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 447 | 1 | Final Synthesis: EtC + Whitening + PBVE | Daedalus II | 257 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 443 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization (gamma_max=0.72) | Daedalus II | 255 | 0.7338 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.780 |\n| 437 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus II | 249 | 0.7341 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.782 |\n| 435 | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=1) | Daedalus II | 248 | 0.7333 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.779 |\n| 432 | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 246 | 0.7335 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.781 |\n| 429 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical\
    \ Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v3) | Daedalus II | 243 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 427 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v2) | Daedalus II | 242 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 426 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE | Daedalus II | 241 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 417 | 1 | EtC + Cross-Batch Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 234 | 0.7101 | 0.722 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.726 | 0.783 |\n| 413 | 1 | EtC + Whitening | Daedalus II | 232 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/simple_batch_transforms.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.special import ndtri\n\ndef _ensure_dense_block(X):\n\
    \    return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\ndef _iter_batches(batches):\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size > 0:\n            yield b, idx\n\ndef apply_brs_inplace(X, batches, gene_mask=None):\n    Xd = _ensure_dense_block(X)\n    n, p = Xd.shape\n    gene_idx = np.arange(p) if gene_mask is None else np.where(gene_mask)[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    for _, idx in _iter_batches(batches):\n        Xb = Xd[idx[:, None], gene_idx]\n        n_b = Xb.shape[0]\n        if n_b <= 1:\n            continue\n        order = np.argsort(Xb, axis=0, kind='mergesort')\n        ranks = np.empty_like(order, dtype=np.int32)\n        cols = np.broadcast_to(np.arange(Xb.shape[1]), order.shape)\n        rows = order\n        ranks[rows, cols] = np.arange(n_b)[:, None]\n        u = (ranks + 0.5) / float(n_b)  # mid-ranks avoid 0/1\n        Z = ndtri(u)\n        Xd[idx[:, None], gene_idx] = Z\n\ndef apply_miqm_inplace(X,\
    \ batches, gene_mask=None, eps=1e-8, rho=1.0):\n    Xd = _ensure_dense_block(X)\n    n, p = Xd.shape\n    gene_idx = np.arange(p) if gene_mask is None else np.where(gene_mask)[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    q1_g = np.quantile(Xd[:, gene_idx], 0.25, axis=0)\n    q3_g = np.quantile(Xd[:, gene_idx], 0.75, axis=0)\n    med_g = np.median(Xd[:, gene_idx], axis=0)\n    iqr_g = np.maximum(q3_g - q1_g, eps)\n    for _, idx in _iter_batches(batches):\n        Xb = Xd[idx[:, None], gene_idx]\n        q1_b = np.quantile(Xb, 0.25, axis=0)\n        q3_b = np.quantile(Xb, 0.75, axis=0)\n        med_b = np.median(Xb, axis=0)\n        iqr_b = np.maximum(q3_b - q1_b, eps)\n        scale = (iqr_g / iqr_b) ** rho\n        Xd[idx[:, None], gene_idx] = (Xb - med_b) * scale + med_g\n\ndef apply_winsor_inplace(X, batches, gene_mask=None, q_low=0.01, q_high=0.99):\n    Xd = _ensure_dense_block(X)\n    n, p = Xd.shape\n    gene_idx = np.arange(p) if gene_mask is None else np.where(gene_mask)[0]\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    for _, idx in _iter_batches(batches):\n        Xb = Xd[idx[:, None], gene_idx]\n        lo = np.quantile(Xb, q_low, axis=0)\n        hi = np.quantile(Xb, q_high, axis=0)\n        Xb = np.minimum(np.maximum(Xb, lo), hi)\n        Xd[idx[:, None], gene_idx] = Xb\n\ndef apply_qmap_global_inplace(X, batches, gene_mask=None, lam=1.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Corrected QMAP: per-gene, per-batch quantile mapping to pooled global distribution.\n    For gene j and batch b with size n_b:\n      - ranks r=0..n_b-1 (stable mergesort)\n      - quantiles q=(r+0.5)/n_b\n      - map to pooled global sorted at positions floor(q*(n-1))\n    Blend: X' = lam * mapped + (1 - lam) * original (on selected genes).\n    \"\"\"\n    Xd = _ensure_dense_block(X)\n    n, p = Xd.shape\n    gene_idx = np.arange(p) if gene_mask is None else np.where(gene_mask)[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    for j in gene_idx:\n        ref_sorted = np.sort(Xd[:,\
    \ j], kind='mergesort')\n        n_ref = ref_sorted.shape[0]\n        x_new = Xd[:, j].copy()\n        for b in uniq:\n            idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n            n_b = idx.size\n            if n_b <= 1:\n                continue\n            xb = Xd[idx, j]\n            order = np.argsort(xb, kind='mergesort')\n            ranks = np.empty_like(order, dtype=np.int64)\n            ranks[order] = np.arange(n_b)\n            q = (ranks + 0.5) / float(n_b)\n            pos = np.clip((q * (n_ref - 1)).astype(np.int64), 0, n_ref - 1)\n            mapped = ref_sorted[pos]\n            x_new[idx] = lam * mapped + (1.0 - lam) * xb\n        Xd[:, j] = x_new\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is\
    \ not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
