    \ | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 467 | 1 | Fix: EtC + Whitening + PBVE (from ID 447) | Daedalus III | 273 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 447 | 1 | Final Synthesis: EtC + Whitening + PBVE | Daedalus II | 257 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 443 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization (gamma_max=0.72) | Daedalus II | 255 | 0.7338 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.780 |\n| 437 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus II | 249 | 0.7341 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.782 |\n| 435 | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=1) | Daedalus II | 248 | 0.7333 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.779 |\n| 432 | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 246 | 0.7335\
    \ | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.781 |\n| 429 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v3) | Daedalus II | 243 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 427 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v2) | Daedalus II | 242 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 426 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE | Daedalus II | 241 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 417 | 1 | EtC + Cross-Batch Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 234 | 0.7101 | 0.722 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.726 | 0.783 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/perbatch_var_equalization.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom numpy.linalg import eigh\nimport anndata\
    \ as ad\n\ndef _center(Z):\n    mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return Z - mu, mu\n\ndef global_soft_whiten(Z: np.ndarray, tau: float = 0.95, eps: float = 1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Soft-whitening of columns by exponent tau in [0,1]:\n      Z_wh = (Z - mean) @ U @ diag((S + eps)^(-tau/2)) @ U.T, where S are eigenvalues of Cov(Z).\n    tau=1.0 gives full whitening; tau=0 reduces to identity.\n    \"\"\"\n    Zc, mu = _center(Z)\n    # Covariance in feature space (d x d), d is small (~64)\n    d = Zc.shape[1]\n    C = (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(1, Zc.shape[0] - 1)\n    # Symmetric EVD\n    S, U = eigh(C)\n    S = np.maximum(S, 0.0)\n    S_pow = np.power(S + eps, -0.5 * tau)\n    T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T  # U @ diag(S_pow) @ U.T\n    Zw = Zc @ T\n    return Zw, mu\n\ndef perbatch_diag_var_equalize(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, alpha: float = 0.3, eps: float = 1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Per-batch diagonal variance equalization in a fixed feature basis:\n      For each PC j, and batch b:\n  \
    \      scale s_bj = (var_all_j / (var_bj + eps))^(alpha/2)\n      Apply: Z_bj := (Z_bj - mu_all_j) * s_bj + mu_all_j\n    alpha in [0,1]; alpha=0 no change; alpha=1 matches per-batch variances to global per PC.\n    \"\"\"\n    Zc, mu = _center(Z)\n    n, d = Z.shape\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    var_all = Zc.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + eps\n\n    Z_eq = Zc.copy()\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = (batches == b)\n        if not np.any(idx):\n            continue\n        Zb = Zc[idx, :]\n        var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + eps\n        s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha)  # shape (d,)\n        Z_eq[idx, :] = Zb * s\n\n    return Z_eq + mu\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed\
    \ as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
