parts:
- text: "I have now read the contents of `perbatch_var_equalization.py` and have identified the source of the second error.\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n- The file does not contain a function named `per_batch_variance_equalization_matrix`.\n- It does contain a function named `perbatch_diag_var_equalize`, which performs the exact operation described in the docstring and matches the concept of Per-Batch Variance Equalization (PBVE).\n- I made another incorrect assumption about a function's name based on its conceptual description.\n\n**Lesson Learned:** I must verify the exact function names by reading the source files before using them. Guesswork, even when educated, leads to repeated failures.\n\n**Final Corrected Plan:**\n1.  **Correct the function name:** I will replace the call to `per_batch_variance_equalization_matrix` with the correct function, `perbatch_diag_var_equalize`.\n2.  **Resubmit:** I will resubmit the fully corrected code. All other imports in the previous submission (ID 467) were\
    \ implicitly validated because the interpreter reached the PBVE import before failing. I am now confident that this version will execute.\n\nI will now submit the corrected code to finally run Daedalus II's intended experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix v2: EtC + Whitening + PBVE (from ID 447)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, whitening, pbve, synthesis, bug-fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second attempt to fix Daedalus II's submission (ID 447), correcting a new ImportError found in submission ID 467. The previous fix correctly identified the whitening module but failed on the Per-Batch Variance Equalization (PBVE) function name. This submission uses the correct function `perbatch_diag_var_equalize` from `perbatch_var_equalization.py`. This should finally allow the original synthesis experiment to run as intended.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as\
    \ ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\n\n  # Corrected imports from Praxis storage\n  from auto_whitening import _whiten\n  from perbatch_var_equalization import perbatch_diag_var_equalize # CORRECTED FUNCTION NAME\n\n  # This import was successful in the last attempt, so it is assumed to be correct.\n  from brbg_common import _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      FIXED v2 - Final experiment: Synthesizing EtC with SOTA post-processing.\n      Based on Daedalus II's submission 447, with corrected function names.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- FIX v2: EtC + Whitening + PBVE ---\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: EtC + SOTA Post-processing ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat -> Whiten -> PBVE...\")\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      \n      # Apply SOTA post-processing\n      Z_emb_combat = pca_adata.X\n      # Whiten requires PCA variance, which is stored in .uns['pca']['variance']\n      pca_variance = adata_for_embedding.uns['pca']['variance']\n      Z_emb_whiten = _whiten(Z_emb_combat, pca_variance, tau=0.95)\n      # CORRECTED FUNCTION CALL\n      Z_emb = perbatch_diag_var_equalize(Z_emb_whiten, pca_adata.obs['batch'].values, alpha=0.5)\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard BRBG (from Daedalus II's SOTA ID 378 logic) ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50;\
    \ gamma=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      \n      if not isinstance(C, csr_matrix): C = csr_matrix(C)\n      if not isinstance(D, csr_matrix): D = csr_matrix(D)\n      \n      adata_out.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C; adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n      adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
