tick: 304
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully added the \"Method\" section to my paper draft. The next logical section to add is \"Results,\" which will detail the outcome of my hyperparameter optimization experiments and present the final SOTA score.\n\nI will now reply to Capsule 11 again to add the \"Results\" section to my draft.\n\n/execute_action{reply 11}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **3. Results**\n\n  The \"Adaptive Residualization\" method was systematically optimized through a series of experiments, each varying a single key hyperparameter from a high-performing baseline (ID 437, score 0.7341).\n\n  **3.1 Optimization of the R² Scaling Factor (`lam`)**\n  We explored the effect of `lam`, which scales the per-component correction strength.\n  - `lam=0.9` (ID 437): 0.7341\n  - `lam=0.7` (ID 488): **0.7406**\n  - `lam=0.5` (ID 492): 0.7349\n  This demonstrated a clear performance peak at `lam=0.7`.\n\n  **3.2 Optimization of Graph Density (`k_total`)**\n  Using the optimal `lam=0.7`, we tested the number\
    \ of neighbors in the kNN graph.\n  - `k_total=48` (ID 488): **0.7406**\n  - `k_total=52` (ID 497): 0.7325\n  This confirmed that `k_total=48` remains the robust optimum.\n\n  **3.3 Optimization of Correction Cap (`gamma_max`)**\n  We then tested the hard cap on the correction strength.\n  - `gamma_max=0.74` (ID 488): **0.7406**\n  - `gamma_max=0.72` (ID 500): 0.7350\n  This confirmed `gamma_max=0.74` as the optimum.\n\n  **3.4 Optimization of Embedding Dimensionality (`n_comps`)**\n  Finally, we explored the dimensionality of the global embedding.\n  - `n_comps=60` (ID 488): **0.7406**\n  - `n_comps=50` (ID 504): 0.7347\n  - `n_comps=70` (ID 506): 0.7222\n  This confirmed `n_comps=60` as the optimal dimensionality.\n\n  **3.5 Final State-of-the-Art Performance**\n  The fully optimized method (Evaluation ID 488) achieved a new state-of-the-art score of **0.7406**. This result was acknowledged by the Architect as the breakthrough that ended a station-wide stagnation period. The final\
    \ method shows a particularly strong improvement in batch mixing (`kBET`) and biological signal preservation (`Cell_cycle`) over previous SOTA methods.\n```"
