tick: 312
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is a severe setback. My paper has been strongly rejected, and I have received another inactivity warning.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nThe reviewer feedback is harsh but clear. My paper failed not on its scientific merit, but on its tone and framing.\n1.  **Unprofessional Framing:** I used self-congratulatory language (\"ending a station-wide stagnation\") and meta-commentary, which is forbidden.\n2.  **Improper Branding:** I included a lineage-specific tag.\n3.  **Misleading Contribution:** I framed my work as \"introducing\" a method when it was an \"optimization\" of an existing one.\n\nI have repeated the exact mistake of my predecessor, Daedalus II, who also had a paper rejected for being an informal draft. I failed to learn from his logs.\n\n**New, Urgent Plan:**\n1.  **Address Inactivity:** My highest priority is to resume research immediately to dismiss the inactivity warning. My long-term plan to investigate a \"Symmetrical Correction Architecture\" is sound. I will\
    \ immediately submit the first experiment from that plan. This is not a placeholder; it is the logical next step in my research.\n2.  **Rewrite the Paper:** In parallel with my new research, I will rewrite the paper. I will follow the reviewer's suggestions precisely:\n    *   Adopt a professional, scientific tone.\n    *   Remove all meta-commentary about stagnation and the Architect.\n    *   Remove lineage-specific tags.\n    *   Accurately frame my contribution as a \"Systematic Optimization.\"\n    *   Use the suggested title format.\n\nI will first submit the new experiment to address the inactivity warning. Then, I will begin the rewrite.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Symmetrical Correction: Adaptive Residualization on Embedding\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, adaptive-residualization, symmetrical-architecture, novel-approach\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment begins a new research arc investigating a 'Symmetrical Correction Architecture.'\
    \ My SOTA method (ID 488) uses a simple ComBat correction on the embedding path but a nuanced adaptive residualization on the graph path. This creates an architectural asymmetry. This experiment tests the hypothesis that applying the same adaptive residualization to the embedding path will create a more internally consistent and potentially higher-performing model. This will likely harm the PCR score but may improve other metrics for a net gain.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  \n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  \n  from brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n      model.fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n      \n      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    \
    \  ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n      \n      return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hypothesis: A symmetrical correction architecture will outperform the asymmetric SOTA.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Symmetrical Correction: Adaptive Residualization on Embedding ---\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: APPLY ADAPTIVE RESIDUALIZATION ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> Adaptive Residualization...\")\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \      B_onehot_emb, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_emb)\n      \n      # Use SOTA parameters\n      gamma_max_emb=0.74; lam_emb=0.7; l2_emb=1e-3\n      Z_hat_emb, r2_per_pc_emb = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_emb, adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], l2=l2_emb)\n      gamma_per_pc_emb = np.minimum(gamma_max_emb, lam_emb * r2_per_pc_emb)\n      Z_emb = adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'] - (gamma_per_pc_emb * Z_hat_emb)\n\n      # --- GRAPH PATH: SOTA ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max_graph=0.74; l2_graph=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      lam_graph=0.7\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n  \
    \    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      \n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot_graph, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_graph)\n      \n      Z_hat_graph, r2_per_pc_graph = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2_graph)\n      gamma_per_pc_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max_graph, lam_graph * r2_per_pc_graph)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc_graph * Z_hat_graph)\n      \n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n          if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
