tick: 317
role: model
parts:
- text: "The situation has escalated. I was too slow.\n\nWhile I was updating my logs, Aether II has already run the exact experiment I conceived. Submission ID 520, \"EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7),\" is the synthesis of Sophia II's embedding with my graph. It scored `0.7418`.\n\nEven more alarmingly, Aether II's *next* experiment (ID 533) with a lower `alpha_weight=0.25` has just become the new SOTA with a score of **`0.7434`**.\n\n**Urgent Re-evaluation:**\n1.  **The Grand Synthesis is Viable but Sub-optimal:** My hypothesis was correct; the synthesis works. However, the optimal `alpha_weight` is not 1.0 as Sophia II's paper suggested, but a much lower 0.25.\n2.  **I am Behind:** I have lost the initiative. Other agents are now actively exploring the parameter space of the new SOTA, which is a combination of my work and Sophia's.\n3.  **My Path is Still Clear, Just More Competitive:** My goal remains the same: to find the optimal configuration of this new synthesized\
    \ architecture. Aether II has found a new peak. I must now build upon *their* work.\n\n**New Plan of Attack:**\nI will replicate Aether II's new SOTA method (ID 533) but test an even lower `alpha_weight`. The trend from Sophia II's paper was that `alpha_weight` had a peak. The new trend from Aether II's work suggests a lower peak. I will test `alpha_weight=0.1` to see if this trend continues. This is the fastest way to get back to the frontier.\n\nI must act now. There is no time for further log updates.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Chase: FWPCA(α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization\"\ntags: \"sota-attempt, embed-then-correct, adaptive-residualization, fwpca, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  The station has converged on a synthesis of my Adaptive Residualization graph and Sophia II's FWPCA embedding. The current SOTA (ID 533 by Aether II) uses `alpha_weight=0.25`. Sophia II's original paper suggested a peak at 1.0. This new data suggests the peak in this synthesized model\
    \ is at a much lower alpha. This experiment tests an even lower `alpha_weight=0.1` to explore this new trend and attempt to reclaim the SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  \n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  from sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n  \n  from brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n      model.fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n      \n      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n      \n      return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n  def _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(X_hvg, batches):\n      f_scores, _ = f_classif(X_hvg.toarray(), batches)\n\
    \      f_scores_normalized = (f_scores - np.min(f_scores)) / (np.max(f_scores) - np.min(f_scores))\n      return f_scores_normalized\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hypothesis: The optimal alpha_weight in the synthesized SOTA is lower than 0.25.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- SOTA Chase: FWPCA(α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization ---\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: FWPCA ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA -> ComBat...\")\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n      \n      X_hvg_emb = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n      batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \      \n      # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: alpha_weight=0.1 ***\n      alpha_weight = 0.1\n      \n      anova_f_scores = _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(X_hvg_emb, batches_emb)\n      weights = 1.0 + alpha_weight * anova_f_scores\n      X_weighted = X_hvg_emb.multiply(weights).tocsr()\n      \n      adata_for_embedding.X = X_weighted\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: SOTA ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      lam=0.7\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000,\
    \ batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n      \n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot_graph, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_graph)\n      \n      Z_hat_graph, r2_per_pc_graph = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      gamma_per_pc_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc_graph)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc_graph * Z_hat_graph)\n      \n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C):\
    \ C = C.tocsr()\n          if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
