tick: 319
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 319\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,795 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 59 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Chase: FWPCA(α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization' (ID: 540) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7347927294533665\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.779\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.353\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.779  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.353\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.840208  ASW_label: 0.537353  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.743259  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999978  Cell_cycle: 0.309773\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 540\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed NaN value propagation in FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) implementation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed with `ValueError: Input X contains NaN. PCA does not accept missing values encoded as NaN natively.`\n\nThe error occurred in the FWPCA embedding path at line 54 when calling `sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)`.\n\n**Root cause analysis:**\n1. The `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores()` function calculates ANOVA F-scores to determine batch effect severity per gene\n2. The `f_classif()` function from sklearn can return NaN values when:\n   - A gene has identical values across all batches (no variance)\n   - Division by zero occurs in the ANOVA calculation\n\
    3. The normalization step `(f_scores - min) / (max - min)` can also produce NaN when all f_scores are identical\n4. These NaN values propagate through:\n   - `weights = 1.0 + alpha_weight * anova_f_scores` (line 29)\n   - `X_weighted = X_hvg_emb.multiply(weights)` (line 30)\n   - `adata_for_embedding.X = X_weighted` (line 31)\n5. When PCA is applied to the NaN-contaminated matrix, it crashes\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores()` function in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. **NaN handling after f_classif:**\n   ```python\n   f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n   ```\n   - Replaces any NaN, inf, or -inf values with 0.0\n   - Ensures all f_scores are finite numbers\n\n2. **Safe normalization:**\n   ```python\n   if f_max - f_min < 1e-10:\n       # If all f_scores are essentially the same, return uniform weights\n       f_scores_normalized = np.zeros_like(f_scores)\n   else:\n       f_scores_normalized = (f_scores - f_min)\
    \ / (f_max - f_min)\n   ```\n   - Prevents division by zero when all f_scores are identical\n   - Returns zero vector (equivalent to no weighting) in degenerate case\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed code ran successfully for >300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The FWPCA + Adaptive Residualization pipeline can now execute through completion\n- The fix preserves the algorithm's intent: genes with no batch effect get zero ANOVA scores and minimal weighting\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe fix is minimal and conservative:\n- NaN values are treated as \"no batch effect\" (score = 0)\n- Uniform f_scores are treated as \"no discriminative information\" (weights = 1.0)\n- The hypothesis test (alpha=0.1 for FWPCA weighting) can now be properly evaluated\n- All other components (ComBat, Adaptive BRBG, balanced KNN) remain unchanged\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them\
    \ manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\ndef _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(X_hvg, batches):\n    f_scores, _ = f_classif(X_hvg.toarray(), batches)\n\n    # Handle NaN values that can occur in f_classif\n    f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    # Avoid\
    \ division by zero in normalization\n    f_min = np.min(f_scores)\n    f_max = np.max(f_scores)\n    if f_max - f_min < 1e-10:\n        # If all f_scores are essentially the same, return uniform weights\n        f_scores_normalized = np.zeros_like(f_scores)\n    else:\n        f_scores_normalized = (f_scores - f_min) / (f_max - f_min)\n\n    return f_scores_normalized\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Hypothesis: The optimal alpha_weight in the synthesized SOTA is lower than 0.25.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- SOTA Chase: FWPCA(α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization ---\")\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: FWPCA ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb\
    \ = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n\n    X_hvg_emb = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: alpha_weight=0.1 ***\n    alpha_weight = 0.1\n\n    anova_f_scores = _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(X_hvg_emb, batches_emb)\n    weights = 1.0 + alpha_weight * anova_f_scores\n    X_weighted = X_hvg_emb.multiply(weights).tocsr()\n\n    adata_for_embedding.X = X_weighted\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n\n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH: SOTA ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    lam=0.7\n\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_graph, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_graph)\n\n    Z_hat_graph, r2_per_pc_graph = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc_graph)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc_graph * Z_hat_graph)\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is\
    \ not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- SOTA Chase: FWPCA(α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization ---\nEmbedding Path: Running FWPCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/25372139-6f2e-45fc-b5b0-22a0cbb5b4df/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 25372139-6f2e-45fc-b5b0-22a0cbb5b4df\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/sklearn/feature_selection/_univariate_selection.py:111: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  f = msb / msw\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization:\
    \ EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA\
