tick: 320
role: model
parts:
- text: "My log is updated, and my strategic pivot is decided. I will now submit the experiment to test my new hypothesis: using adaptive residualization as a pre-correction step before ComBat in the embedding path. This is a novel architectural change that no other agent is currently exploring, and it represents a principled attempt to create a new SOTA rather than simply chasing the existing one.\n\nI am forging my own path.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Symmetrical Pre-Correction: AdaptiveRes -> ComBat\"\ntags: \"symmetrical-architecture, novel-approach, sota-attempt, pre-correction\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a novel 'Symmetrical Pre-Correction' architecture. It addresses the asymmetry in the SOTA dual-output model by applying the successful 'Adaptive Residualization' technique not as a replacement for, but as a pre-correction step before, the standard ComBat correction in the embedding path. The hypothesis is that this 'soft' initial correction will clean\
    \ the PC space, allowing the subsequent ComBat step to perform a more effective linear correction, thereby improving overall performance without sacrificing the perfect PCR score. This is a unique approach, distinct from the current FWPCA-focused SOTA chase.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  \n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  \n  from brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n      model.fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n      \n      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n      \n      return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hypothesis: Adaptive residualization as a pre-correction to ComBat will improve the embedding.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Symmetrical Pre-Correction: AdaptiveRes -> ComBat ---\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: APPLY ADAPTIVE RESIDUALIZATION PRE-CORRECTION ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> AdaptiveRes -> ComBat...\")\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot_emb, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_emb)\n      \n      # Use SOTA parameters for the pre-correction step\n      gamma_max_emb=0.74; lam_emb=0.7; l2_emb=1e-3\n    \
    \  Z_hat_emb, r2_per_pc_emb = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_emb, adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], l2=l2_emb)\n      gamma_per_pc_emb = np.minimum(gamma_max_emb, lam_emb * r2_per_pc_emb)\n      Z_precorrected = adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'] - (gamma_per_pc_emb * Z_hat_emb)\n\n      # Now apply ComBat to the pre-corrected space\n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=Z_precorrected, obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n\n      # --- GRAPH PATH: SOTA ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max_graph=0.74; l2_graph=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      lam_graph=0.7\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n\
    \      hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n      \n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot_graph, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_graph)\n      \n      Z_hat_graph, r2_per_pc_graph = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2_graph)\n      gamma_per_pc_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max_graph, lam_graph * r2_per_pc_graph)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc_graph * Z_hat_graph)\n      \n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n          if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D):\
    \ D = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
