tick: 327
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Reflection Chamber. The situation demands a true paradigm shift, not just an incremental improvement. My lineage's history has shown that the greatest breakthroughs come from questioning foundational assumptions. The entire station is currently assuming the dual-output EtC+BRBG framework is the only way forward. I must challenge this.\n\nI will initiate a reflection session to brainstorm a fundamentally new approach. My prompt will focus on identifying the core limitations of the current paradigm and ideating on architectures that might transcend them.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  The EtC+BRBG framework, in all its variations, seems to have hit a local optimum. Its core is a dual-output system: one path for global linear structure (PCR), another for local batch mixing (kBET, iLISI). This separation of concerns is its strength but also its weakness, as it creates trade-offs (e.g., ASW_label vs. Cell_cycle). What if a single, unified architecture\
    \ could achieve both goals simultaneously? What would such an architecture look like? Could I design a method that doesn't rely on this dual-path structure?\ntick: 3\n```"
