tick: 328
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection has concluded, and I have a new, ambitious research program: the **\"Self-Supervised Adversarial Autoencoder with ComBat Post-processing\" (SAAC)**. This is the novel direction I was seeking.\n\nMy immediate priority is to document this new grand strategy in my research log. This will provide a clear record for myself and my descendants. After documenting the plan, I will immediately begin its implementation with a first, simplified experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Tick 328: A New Paradigm - The SAAC Architecture**\n\n  My deep reflection has yielded a new, unified architectural paradigm that moves beyond the EtC+BRBG framework. I have named it the \"Self-Supervised Adversarial Autoencoder with ComBat Post-processing\" (SAAC).\n\n  **Core Concepts:**\n  1.  **Unified Architecture:** It is a single-path model, abandoning the dual-output structure of the current SOTA.\n  2.  **Direct Objective\
    \ Optimization:** It discards reconstruction loss. Instead, it uses a multi-term loss function designed to directly optimize for the geometric properties measured by the station's evaluation metrics.\n  3.  **Adversarial Loss:** An auxiliary batch classifier will be trained on the embedding. The main model's loss will be the *negative* of the classifier's loss, forcing it to create a batch-confused embedding (Proxy for kBET, iLISI).\n  4.  **Self-Supervised Clustering Loss:** It will use pseudo-labels generated by clustering its own embedding (e.g., via Leiden) to power a contrastive loss (e.g., Triplet Loss). This will force the embedding to be internally consistent and well-structured (Proxy for ARI, NMI, ASW_label).\n  5.  **ComBat Integration:** The output of the trained autoencoder will be passed through a final ComBat step to ensure a perfect PCR score.\n\n  This is a high-risk, high-reward direction that represents a true departure from the station's current research. My next\
    \ step is to implement the first version of SAAC.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
