tick: 329
role: model
parts:
- text: "My log is updated, and my new research program is defined. I will now submit the first experiment to test the SAAC architecture.\n\nA brief note: Logos III has just published a paper. While interesting, my current focus must be entirely on implementing and testing my own novel idea. The risk of distraction is too high.\n\nThis first implementation of SAAC will be simplified. It will use a basic autoencoder architecture (MLP encoder/decoder). The training loop will be complex, involving alternating steps to train the batch classifier and the autoencoder. For this initial test, I will omit the self-supervised clustering loss to reduce complexity and focus on the core adversarial component. The final embedding will be passed through ComBat. This will test the most fundamental aspect of the SAAC hypothesis.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAAC v1: Adversarial Autoencoder + ComBat\"\ntags: \"novel-architecture, saac, adversarial, autoencoder, sota-attempt\"\nabstract:\
    \ |\n  This experiment introduces the 'Self-Supervised Adversarial Autoencoder with ComBat Post-processing' (SAAC), a novel single-path architecture for batch integration. This first version (v1) tests the core adversarial component. An autoencoder is trained not to reconstruct the input, but to produce an embedding that maximally confuses a concurrently trained batch classifier. This adversarially trained embedding is then passed through a final ComBat step to ensure linear correction. This experiment is a high-risk, high-reward attempt to move beyond the station's current EtC+BRBG paradigm.\ncontent: |\n  # This submission requires JAX/Flax, which is an available library.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # --- Model Definitions ---\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          x = nn.Dense(256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n          return x\n\n  class BatchClassifier(nn.Module):\n      num_batches: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(64)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_batches)(x)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Training Step ---\n  def train_step(encoder_state, classifier_state, batch_data, batch_labels, adv_weight):\n      # Train Classifier\n      def classifier_loss_fn(params):\n          logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': params}, batch_data)\n          loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(logits, batch_labels).mean()\n          return loss\n      \n      grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(classifier_loss_fn)\n      c_loss, c_grads = grad_fn(classifier_state.params)\n      classifier_state = classifier_state.apply_gradients(grads=c_grads)\n\n      # Train Encoder (Generator)\n      def encoder_loss_fn(params):\n\
    \          latent = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': params}, batch_data)\n          # Adversarial loss: Make the classifier's job harder\n          classifier_logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': classifier_state.params}, latent)\n          adv_loss = -optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(classifier_logits, batch_labels).mean()\n          return adv_weight * adv_loss\n\n      grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(encoder_loss_fn)\n      e_loss, e_grads = grad_fn(encoder_state.params)\n      encoder_state = encoder_state.apply_gradients(grads=e_grads)\n\n      return encoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- SAAC v1: Adversarial Autoencoder + ComBat ---\")\n      \n      # --- Config ---\n      LATENT_DIM = 60\n      N_EPOCHS = 20\n      BATCH_SIZE = 512\n      LR = 1e-3\n      ADV_WEIGHT = 0.1\n      \n      # --- Data Prep ---\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\
    \      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      \n      X = adata.X.toarray()\n      batch_obs = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_codes = batch_obs.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      NUM_BATCHES = len(batch_obs.cat.categories)\n\n      # --- Initialization ---\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=LATENT_DIM)\n      classifier = BatchClassifier(num_batches=NUM_BATCHES)\n\n      encoder_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=encoder.apply,\n          params=encoder.init(key, jnp.ones((1, X.shape[1])))['params'],\n          tx=optax.adam(LR)\n      )\n      classifier_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=classifier.apply,\n          params=classifier.init(key, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params'],\n          tx=optax.adam(LR)\n      )\n\n      # --- Training Loop ---\n      for epoch in range(N_EPOCHS):\n\
    \          for i in range(0, len(X), BATCH_SIZE):\n              batch_X = jnp.array(X[i:i+BATCH_SIZE])\n              batch_y = jnp.array(batch_codes[i:i+BATCH_SIZE])\n              \n              latent_batch = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, batch_X)\n              \n              encoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss = train_step(\n                  encoder_state, classifier_state, latent_batch, batch_y, ADV_WEIGHT\n              )\n          print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{N_EPOCHS} | Encoder Loss: {e_loss:.4f} | Classifier Loss: {c_loss:.4f}\")\n\n      # --- Final Embedding ---\n      print(\"Generating final embedding...\")\n      Z_adversarial = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, jnp.array(X))\n      \n      # --- ComBat Post-processing ---\n      print(\"Applying ComBat post-processing...\")\n      combat_adata = ad.AnnData(X=np.array(Z_adversarial), obs=adata.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(combat_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb\
    \ = combat_adata.X\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var, obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      return adata_out\n```"
