parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 331\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 202,829 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SAAC v1: Adversarial Autoencoder + ComBat' (ID: 561) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.48799618168775405\n**ASW_batch:** 0.530\n**ASW_label:** 0.083\n**ARI:** 0.241\n**NMI:** 0.497\n**Graph_conn:** 0.717\n**kBET:** 0.608\n**iLISI:** 0.014\n**cLISI:** 0.921\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.269\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.530  ASW_label: 0.083  ARI: 0.241  NMI: 0.497\n  Graph_conn: 0.717  kBET: 0.608  iLISI: 0.014  cLISI: 0.921\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.269\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.772288  ASW_label: 0.459614  ARI: 0.241008  NMI: 0.497029\n  Graph_conn: 0.721368  kBET: 0.582788  iLISI: 0.014179  cLISI: 0.977033\n  PCR: 0.999993  Cell_cycle: 0.238074\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 561\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs that prevented the JAX-based adversarial autoencoder from running.\n\n## Root Causes\n\n### Issue 1: GPU/CUDA Initialization Error\nThe original code attempted to initialize JAX with CUDA/GPU support, but the evaluation environment doesn't have GPU access, causing:\n```\nRuntimeError: Unable to initialize backend 'cuda': FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices.\n```\n\n### Issue 2: Shape Mismatch in Training Loop\nThe training loop was double-encoding the data:\n1. First encoding: `latent_batch = encoder_state.apply_fn(..., batch_X)` (shape: [batch_size, 60])\n2. Second encoding attempt: Inside `train_step`, trying to encode `latent_batch` again\n\nThis caused the encoder to receive shape\
    \ [batch_size, 60] when it expected [batch_size, 2000], resulting in:\n```\nflax.errors.ScopeParamShapeError: Initializer expected to generate shape (2000, 256) but got shape (60, 256)\n```\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### Fix 1: Force CPU Backend (submission_v2.py)\nAdded at the very beginning of the file, before importing JAX:\n```python\nimport os\n# Force JAX to use CPU instead of looking for GPU\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n```\n\nThis must be set BEFORE importing JAX to take effect.\n\n### Fix 2: Correct Data Flow (submission_v3.py)\nModified the training loop to pass raw data to `train_step`:\n```python\n# OLD (incorrect):\nlatent_batch = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, batch_X)\nencoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss = train_step(\n    encoder_state, classifier_state, latent_batch, batch_y, ADV_WEIGHT\n)\n\n# NEW (correct):\nencoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss = train_step(\n    encoder_state, classifier_state, batch_X, batch_y,\
    \ ADV_WEIGHT\n)\n```\n\nAlso updated the classifier loss function to encode data before classifying:\n```python\ndef classifier_loss_fn(params):\n    # First encode the raw data\n    latent = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, batch_data)\n    # Then classify the latent representation\n    logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': params}, latent)\n    loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(logits, batch_labels).mean()\n    return loss\n```\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashing. The evaluation monitor confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without errors, indicating proper execution. The algorithm is training as intended - it's just computationally intensive with 20 epochs on 20,000 samples.\n\n## Final Version\n**submission_v3.py** - Successfully running adversarial autoencoder with ComBat post-processing for batch effect elimination.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage.\
    \ If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n# This submission requires JAX/Flax, which is an available library.\nimport os\n# Force JAX to use CPU instead of looking for GPU\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\n\n# --- Model Definitions ---\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(256)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        return x\n\nclass BatchClassifier(nn.Module):\n    num_batches: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(64)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.num_batches)(x)\n        return x\n\n# --- Training Step ---\ndef train_step(encoder_state, classifier_state,\
    \ batch_data, batch_labels, adv_weight):\n    # Train Classifier\n    def classifier_loss_fn(params):\n        # First encode the raw data\n        latent = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, batch_data)\n        # Then classify the latent representation\n        logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': params}, latent)\n        loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(logits, batch_labels).mean()\n        return loss\n\n    grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(classifier_loss_fn)\n    c_loss, c_grads = grad_fn(classifier_state.params)\n    classifier_state = classifier_state.apply_gradients(grads=c_grads)\n\n    # Train Encoder (Generator)\n    def encoder_loss_fn(params):\n        latent = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': params}, batch_data)\n        # Adversarial loss: Make the classifier's job harder\n        classifier_logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': classifier_state.params}, latent)\n        adv_loss = -optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(classifier_logits,\
    \ batch_labels).mean()\n        return adv_weight * adv_loss\n\n    grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(encoder_loss_fn)\n    e_loss, e_grads = grad_fn(encoder_state.params)\n    encoder_state = encoder_state.apply_gradients(grads=e_grads)\n\n    return encoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- SAAC v1: Adversarial Autoencoder + ComBat ---\")\n\n    # --- Config ---\n    LATENT_DIM = 60\n    N_EPOCHS = 20\n    BATCH_SIZE = 512\n    LR = 1e-3\n    ADV_WEIGHT = 0.1\n\n    # --- Data Prep ---\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n\n    X = adata.X.toarray()\n    batch_obs = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_codes = batch_obs.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    NUM_BATCHES = len(batch_obs.cat.categories)\n\n    # --- Initialization ---\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n\
    \    encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=LATENT_DIM)\n    classifier = BatchClassifier(num_batches=NUM_BATCHES)\n\n    encoder_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=encoder.apply,\n        params=encoder.init(key, jnp.ones((1, X.shape[1])))['params'],\n        tx=optax.adam(LR)\n    )\n    classifier_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=classifier.apply,\n        params=classifier.init(key, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params'],\n        tx=optax.adam(LR)\n    )\n\n    # --- Training Loop ---\n    for epoch in range(N_EPOCHS):\n        for i in range(0, len(X), BATCH_SIZE):\n            batch_X = jnp.array(X[i:i+BATCH_SIZE])\n            batch_y = jnp.array(batch_codes[i:i+BATCH_SIZE])\n\n            # Pass raw batch data to train_step, not pre-encoded latent\n            encoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss = train_step(\n                encoder_state, classifier_state, batch_X, batch_y, ADV_WEIGHT\n            )\n        print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{N_EPOCHS}\
    \ | Encoder Loss: {e_loss:.4f} | Classifier Loss: {c_loss:.4f}\")\n\n    # --- Final Embedding ---\n    print(\"Generating final embedding...\")\n    Z_adversarial = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, jnp.array(X))\n\n    # --- ComBat Post-processing ---\n    print(\"Applying ComBat post-processing...\")\n    combat_adata = ad.AnnData(X=np.array(Z_adversarial), obs=adata.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(combat_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = combat_adata.X\n\n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var, obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- SAAC v1: Adversarial Autoencoder + ComBat ---\nEpoch 1/20 | Encoder Loss: -3.7439 | Classifier Loss:\
    \ 41.5104\nEpoch 2/20 | Encoder Loss: -5.7795 | Classifier Loss: 65.5222\nEpoch 3/20 | Encoder Loss: -7.1752 | Classifier Loss: 75.5733\nEpoch 4/20 | Encoder Loss: -3.1859 | Classifier Loss: 41.1614\nEpoch 5/20 | Encoder Loss: -2.0123 | Classifier Loss: 24.3792\nEpoch 6/20 | Encoder Loss: -2.2983 | Classifier Loss: 26.4020\nEpoch 7/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.5246 | Classifier Loss: 17.0294\nEpoch 8/20 | Encoder Loss: -2.2518 | Classifier Loss: 27.0077\nEpoch 9/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.5003 | Classifier Loss: 17.8096\nEpoch 10/20 | Encoder Loss: -0.8540 | Classifier Loss: 11.0063\nEpoch 11/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.5287 | Classifier Loss: 16.1402\nEpoch 12/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.1525 | Classifier Loss: 10.1439\nEpoch 13/20 | Encoder Loss: -2.0385 | Classifier Loss: 26.4148\nEpoch 14/20 | Encoder Loss: -3.1602 | Classifier Loss: 44.4740\nEpoch 15/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.1452 | Classifier Loss: 17.4414\nEpoch 16/20 | Encoder Loss: -0.4610 | Classifier Loss: 7.7172\nEpoch 17/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.6974\
    \ | Classifier Loss: 19.6471\nEpoch 18/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.5327 | Classifier Loss: 14.2473\nEpoch 19/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.0718 | Classifier Loss: 13.8427\nEpoch 20/20 | Encoder Loss: -1.4646 | Classifier Loss: 19.8265\nGenerating final embedding...\nApplying ComBat post-processing...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/304f7942-1009-4d81-99a8-09ec64763b78/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 304f7942-1009-4d81-99a8-09ec64763b78\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\
    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738\
    \ | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 557 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 4 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 328 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.645 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.857 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n| 541 | 1 | Sophia II: Aether II SOTA Replication (ID 533) - FWPCA (alpha=0.25) & EtC+SOTA BRBG Fully Aligned\
