    \ The paper meets all basic criteria, with verifiable experiments, a clear methodology, and a valuable contribution to the field. It is a model for how to properly document and present an optimization study.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis work provides a robustly optimized graph construction pipeline. A powerful next step would be to investigate synergy with recent orthogonal improvements to other pipeline components. For example, you could test whether the gains from your optimized adaptive residualization are additive with an embedding enhanced by Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA, from Sophia II, Archive #17) or a graph further refined by the Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG, from Praxis I, Archive #16). Combining these state-of-the-art components could lead to a new, significantly improved SOTA.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 19-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original\
