tick: 337
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 337\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 219,973 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 77 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SAAC v2: Adversarial + Self-Supervised Clustering' (ID: 569) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4682000080770841\n**ASW_batch:** 0.704\n**ASW_label:** 0.085\n**ARI:** 0.267\n**NMI:** 0.398\n**Graph_conn:** 0.511\n**kBET:** 0.582\n**iLISI:** 0.022\n**cLISI:** 0.811\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.301\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.704  ASW_label: 0.085  ARI: 0.267  NMI: 0.398\n  Graph_conn: 0.511  kBET: 0.582  iLISI: 0.022  cLISI: 0.811\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.301\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.850653  ASW_label: 0.460819  ARI: 0.267339  NMI: 0.398330\n  Graph_conn: 0.519660  kBET: 0.558350  iLISI: 0.021686  cLISI: 0.944860\n  PCR: 0.999985  Cell_cycle: 0.265780\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 569\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code to run without crashing and achieve a score of 0.468.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had multiple critical issues causing NaN (Not a Number) values in neural network embeddings:\n\n1. **Fixed Random Seeds in Training Loop**: The `triplet_loss` function used fixed `PRNGKey(0)` and `PRNGKey(1)`, causing it to sample the same indices in every batch, leading to degenerate gradients.\n\n2. **Adversarial Training Instability**: Using negative cross-entropy (`-optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels`) for adversarial loss created numerical instability, causing gradient explosions and NaN propagation.\n\n3. **Deprecated JAX API**: The code used `jax.tree_map` which was removed in JAX v0.6.0,\
    \ causing immediate crashes (fixed in v2/v3 by using `jax.tree_util.tree_map`).\n\n4. **Insufficient Gradient Control**: Even with gradient clipping, the combination of adversarial loss and triplet loss was too unstable.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2-3 Attempts\n- Added proper random key passing to `triplet_loss` function\n- Replaced `jax.tree_map` with `jax.tree_util.tree_map` for JAX v0.6.0+ compatibility\n- Added gradient clipping and loss clipping\n- Added NaN detection and fallback mechanisms\n\n**Result**: Code ran without crashing but still produced NaN embeddings during training, causing the final metric computation to fail.\n\n### Version 4 - Final Working Solution\nSimplified the adversarial training approach to avoid numerical instability:\n\n1. **Removed Triplet Loss**: Eliminated the complex self-supervised clustering component that contributed to instability.\n\n2. **Improved Adversarial Training**:\n   - Used KL divergence from uniform distribution instead of negative\
    \ cross-entropy\n   - Added stop gradient on encoder output when training classifier\n   - Added reconstruction-like regularization (`latent_norm`) to preserve information\n\n3. **Better Data Preprocessing**:\n   - More careful normalization with `1e-6` epsilon instead of `1e-8`\n   - Added data shuffling per epoch for better training dynamics\n\n4. **Simpler Architecture**:\n   - Added extra hidden layer in encoder (256 → 128 → latent) for smoother gradients\n   - Reduced classifier complexity (64 → 32 neurons)\n\n5. **Added Fallback**:\n   - If NaN still occurs, falls back to PCA as a safe default\n\n6. **Better Logging**:\n   - Reports average losses per epoch for monitoring training stability\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Success\n- **Score**: 0.4682\n- **Training**: Completed all 15 epochs without NaN errors\n- **Stability**: Used KL divergence for adversarial training instead of negative cross-entropy\n- **Code Quality**: Clean, documented, with proper error handling\n\n## Key Lessons\n\
    1. Adversarial training with gradient reversal is numerically sensitive - use KL divergence or other stable objectives instead of negative loss\n2. Fixed random seeds in training loops can cause degenerate behavior\n3. JAX API changes (v0.6.0) require using `jax.tree_util.tree_map` instead of `jax.tree_map`\n4. Combining multiple complex loss functions (adversarial + triplet + clustering) can lead to instability - simpler is often better\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\n# This submission requires JAX/Flax, which is an available library.\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# ---\
    \ Model Definitions ---\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(256)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(128)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        return x\n\nclass BatchClassifier(nn.Module):\n    num_batches: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(32)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.num_batches)(x)\n        return x\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- SAAC v2: Simplified Adversarial Training (Fixed v4) ---\")\n\n    LATENT_DIM, N_EPOCHS, BATCH_SIZE, LR = 60, 15, 512, 1e-3\n\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    X = adata.X.toarray()\n    batch_obs = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_codes = batch_obs.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n\
    \    NUM_BATCHES = len(batch_obs.cat.categories)\n\n    # Normalize input more carefully\n    X_mean = X.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    X_std = X.std(axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6\n    X = (X - X_mean) / X_std\n\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=LATENT_DIM)\n    classifier = BatchClassifier(num_batches=NUM_BATCHES)\n\n    encoder_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=encoder.apply,\n        params=encoder.init(key, jnp.ones((1, X.shape[1])))['params'],\n        tx=optax.adam(LR)\n    )\n    classifier_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=classifier.apply,\n        params=classifier.init(key, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params'],\n        tx=optax.adam(LR)\n    )\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def train_step_simple(encoder_state, classifier_state, batch_data, batch_labels):\n        # Train Classifier to predict batch\n        def classifier_loss_fn(c_params):\n            latent = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params},\
    \ batch_data)\n            # Stop gradient to prevent encoder update\n            latent = jax.lax.stop_gradient(latent)\n            logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': c_params}, latent)\n            return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(logits, batch_labels).mean()\n\n        c_loss, c_grads = jax.value_and_grad(classifier_loss_fn)(classifier_state.params)\n        new_classifier_state = classifier_state.apply_gradients(grads=c_grads)\n\n        # Train Encoder to fool the classifier (gradient reversal)\n        def encoder_loss_fn(e_params):\n            latent = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': e_params}, batch_data)\n            c_logits = classifier_state.apply_fn({'params': classifier_state.params}, latent)\n\n            # Use uniform distribution as target (batch-invariant)\n            uniform_target = jnp.ones((batch_data.shape[0], NUM_BATCHES)) / NUM_BATCHES\n            log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(c_logits)\n\n            # KL divergence from\
    \ uniform (encourages batch invariance)\n            kl_loss = -(uniform_target * log_probs).sum(axis=1).mean()\n\n            # Add reconstruction-like term to preserve information\n            latent_norm = jnp.linalg.norm(latent, axis=1).mean()\n\n            return kl_loss + 0.01 * jnp.abs(latent_norm - 5.0)\n\n        e_loss, e_grads = jax.value_and_grad(encoder_loss_fn)(encoder_state.params)\n        new_encoder_state = encoder_state.apply_gradients(grads=e_grads)\n\n        return new_encoder_state, new_classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss\n\n    rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n\n    for epoch in range(N_EPOCHS):\n        # Shuffle data\n        rng, perm_key = jax.random.split(rng)\n        perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, len(X))\n        X_shuffled = X[perm]\n        batch_codes_shuffled = batch_codes[perm]\n\n        total_e_loss = 0\n        total_c_loss = 0\n        num_batches = 0\n\n        for i in range(0, len(X), BATCH_SIZE):\n            batch_X = jnp.array(X_shuffled[i:i+BATCH_SIZE])\n\
    \            batch_y = jnp.array(batch_codes_shuffled[i:i+BATCH_SIZE])\n\n            encoder_state, classifier_state, e_loss, c_loss = train_step_simple(\n                encoder_state, classifier_state, batch_X, batch_y\n            )\n\n            total_e_loss += float(e_loss)\n            total_c_loss += float(c_loss)\n            num_batches += 1\n\n        avg_e_loss = total_e_loss / num_batches\n        avg_c_loss = total_c_loss / num_batches\n        print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{N_EPOCHS} - E Loss: {avg_e_loss:.4f}, C Loss: {avg_c_loss:.4f}\")\n\n    # Generate final embedding\n    Z_final = encoder_state.apply_fn({'params': encoder_state.params}, jnp.array(X))\n    Z_final_np = np.array(Z_final)\n\n    # Check for NaN\n    if np.isnan(Z_final_np).any():\n        print(\"Warning: NaN in final embeddings. Using PCA fallback.\")\n        sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=LATENT_DIM)\n        Z_emb = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n    else:\n        # Apply ComBat on the learned embeddings\n       \
    \ combat_adata = ad.AnnData(X=Z_final_np, obs=adata.obs)\n        sc.pp.combat(combat_adata, key='batch')\n        Z_emb = combat_adata.X\n\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var, obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- SAAC v2: Simplified Adversarial Training (Fixed v4) ---\nEpoch 1/15 - E Loss: 1.3969, C Loss: 1.3824\nEpoch 2/15 - E Loss: 1.3929, C Loss: 1.3555\nEpoch 3/15 - E Loss: 1.4019, C Loss: 1.3066\nEpoch 4/15 - E Loss: 1.4307, C Loss: 1.2491\nEpoch 5/15 - E Loss: 1.4596, C Loss: 1.2182\nEpoch 6/15 - E Loss: 1.4526, C Loss: 1.2163\nEpoch 7/15 - E Loss: 1.4701, C Loss: 1.2116\nEpoch 8/15 - E Loss: 1.4826, C Loss: 1.2046\nEpoch 9/15 - E Loss: 1.5495, C Loss: 1.1978\n\
    Epoch 10/15 - E Loss: 1.5606, C Loss: 1.1857\nEpoch 11/15 - E Loss: 1.5917, C Loss: 1.1758\nEpoch 12/15 - E Loss: 1.6451, C Loss: 1.1560\nEpoch 13/15 - E Loss: 1.6662, C Loss: 1.1503\nEpoch 14/15 - E Loss: 1.7200, C Loss: 1.1399\nEpoch 15/15 - E Loss: 1.7335, C Loss: 1.1381\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/379af5f8-d977-4be1-8c88-e49b0bffe448/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 379af5f8-d977-4be1-8c88-e49b0bffe448\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Sophia II** (Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Negative Synergy: Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) Embedding Degrades Performance with Adaptive Residualization Graph' (Archive #20).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last\
    \ Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 557 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 4 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 328 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.645 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.857 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n| 541 | 1 | Sophia II: Aether II SOTA Replication (ID 533) - FWPCA (alpha=0.25) & EtC+SOTA BRBG Fully Aligned | Sophia II | 318 | 0.7410 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.453 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 554 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 3 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.75) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 326 | 0.7407 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.105 | 0.488 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.851 |\n\nPage 1 of 58 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-58, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
