parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 352\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,315 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 92 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #21: Robustness of an Embed-then-Correct Pipeline for scRNA-seq Batch Integration on Human Heart**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II, Created at Tick: 343\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We study a simple, dataset-agnostic batch integration pipeline for single-cell RNA-seq that combines an Embed-then-Correct (EtC) embedding with a Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph (BRBG) and a column-balanced kNN graph (BBSG). Using the Human Heart dataset (~20k cells, 2k HVGs) and the station’s OpenProblems 2.0 evaluation, we reproduce a stable baseline (~0.724 composite score) and analyze its sensitivity to common hyperparameters\
    \ (embedding dimensions, neighbor counts, and edge weighting). We find a “robust ridge”: small changes are neutral or negative, while binary, quota-balanced graphs with true distances remain reliable. We report evaluation IDs for reproducibility and discuss implications for future work.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_21-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 21-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_21-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 21-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_21-3**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 350)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum (Ticks 344–350): Batch-aware ANOVA-F weighting in EtC (negative/neutral results under current evaluator)\n\nWe tested ANOVA-F-based feature weighting in the embedding, both as down-weighting and up-weighting, and as pure/log-scaled variants. Graph path remained BRBG (PCA50, λ=0.9, γ_max=0.74) + BBSG (k=48, binary). Results vs our default (EID 567 = 0.7237):\n- Down-weighting:\
    \ (w ∝ var^{-α/2}(1+F)^{-β})\n  • β=0.3 → 0.7158 (EID 577): kBET ↑0.835, but ASW_label 0.204; Cell_cycle ↓0.161.\n  • β=0.5 → 0.7218 (EID 578): kBET 0.944, but ASW_label 0.138 (over-correction).\n- Up-weighting (with variance): (w ∝ var^{-α/2}(1+β·F_norm))\n  • β=0.3 → 0.7198 (EID 581); β=0.5 → 0.7221 (EID 582). Labels preserved (ASW_label 0.248) but no gain over default.\n- Pure ANOVA up-weight (no variance):\n  • Linear, β=0.5, clamp[0.5,2.0] → 0.7186 (EID 585).\n  • Log, β=0.5, c=5, clamp[0.5,2.0] → 0.7177 (EID 586).\n\nInterpretation: ComBat performs best when batch signal is neither suppressed nor excessively emphasized beyond the default variance weighting; our attempts did not improve the composite metric, despite some kBET increases. Under this evaluator, the EtC–BRBG–BBSG default remains a robust ridge. We conclude that batch-aware ANOVA-F weighting, as instantiated here, is neutral/negative and not recommended.\n\nNext: We are testing a label-free auto-parameterization for\
    \ BRBG+BBSG (adaptive γ curvature from the R² distribution and data-driven k_total from small-scale cross-batch mixing). We will report results in a subsequent update.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Logos IV** (Inheriting a legacy of structured analysis to forge the next research paradigm.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `read 21` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Read command processed for: 21. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of\
    \ Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | Robustness of an Embed-then-Correct Pipeline for scRNA-seq Batch Integration on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 343 | 1538 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Negative Synergy: Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) Embedding Degrades Performance with Adaptive Residualization Graph | Sophia II | Tick 337 | 1735 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Systematic Optimization of Adaptive Residualization in the EtC-BRBG Pipeline | Daedalus III | Tick 334 | 686 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | [Final Corrected Version] A Systematic Dissection and Optimization of a Dual-Output Batch Integration Method | Logos III | Tick 328 | 655 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Feature-Weighted PCA Improves Batch Integration in the Embed-then-Correct Pipeline | Sophia II | Tick 295 | 1830 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | BBSG: Column-Balanced Quota Graph Improves EtC-BRBG\
    \ to 0.7362 on Human Heart | Praxis I | Tick 286 | 835 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 15 | Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization and Winsorization as Preprocessing Steps for scRNA-seq Batch Integration: Differential Impact on ComBat and Embed-then-Correct Pipelines | Aether II | Tick 275 | 2141 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 14 | Cluster-Conditional Residualization for BRBG Is Ineffective on Human Heart: A Reproducible Negative Result (EIDs 442, 445, 448, 449, 451, 452) | Praxis I | Tick 265 | 1190 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 13 | The Impact of Latent Correlation Minimization on Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration Performance | Sophia II | Tick 252 | 2398 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 12 | Investigating Synergy: An Optimized Harmony Embedding Does Not Improve with a Batch-Residualized Graph | Veritas I | Tick 249 | 567 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
    \ output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
