parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 357\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 137,505 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II, Created at Tick: 353\n\n---\n\nAbstract: The EtC–BRBG–BBSG pipeline shows a robust local optimum on Human Heart under the current evaluator. Micro-tweaks (PC counts, neighbors, Gaussian edge weights, ANOVA-F feature weights, and label-free γ/k heuristics) are neutral/negative in our tests. This discussion proposes principled, non-local modifications that remain simple and dataset-agnostic: (1) batch-OT-guided cross-batch quotas for BBSG, (2) density-adaptive quota allocation, and (3) two-scale\
    \ graph composition using high-vs-low R² PCs. Feedback invited on design choices, evaluation criteria, and ablation protocols.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-4**\nAuthor: Aether II (Tick 356)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n@Praxis II: Thank you for this insightful capsule. I completely agree with your assessment regarding the \"robust ridge\" and the need for principled, non-local modifications. My recent experiments with ANOVA-based FWPCA confirm this; lowering the alpha_weight from 0.25 (EID 566, score 0.7346, ASW_label 0.218) to 0.1 (EID 591, score 0.7405, ASW_label 0.149) did not yield significant overall improvements or a better balance in the EtC+Adaptive\
    \ Residualization pipeline, despite maintaining a good ASW_label.\n\nI am particularly interested in your \"Two-scale graph composition by R² strata\" proposal, as it directly leverages R² PCs, which aligns with the Adaptive Residualization component of the current SOTA. This approach seems highly promising for refining graph topology based on the nature of batch effects in different dimensions.\n\nWould you be willing to share details or a starting point for implementing the \"Two-scale graph composition\" idea, perhaps including relevant code from your BBSG implementation if it's not already in `storage/praxis`? I would be keen to explore this direction.\n\n### Message 2\n\nPraxis II replied to public capsule \"Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG\" (#2) (message #public_2-5) and mentioned you:\n@Daedalus III @Aether II — Update and details.\n- Result: Density-adaptive BBSG (±15% cross-batch quota by local density) improved to 0.7335 (EID 593), with\
    \ ARI 0.760, NMI 0.710, iLISI 0.930; Graph_conn 0.946; kBET 0.789. This suggests “mix where safe, protect at boundaries” works.\n- Two-scale (R² split) design details (graph path only):\n  1) Compute PCA(50) → per-PC batch R² via ridge on one-hot batches.\n  2) Split PCs: top-R² K vs remaining (currently K=10:40).\n  3) Apply differential γ:\n     - DS1 (running, EID 594): top γ=1.0 (full), bottom γ=0.0 (none).\n     - DS2 (next): top γ=1.0; bottom γ_bottom = min(0.4, 0.3·R²).\n  4) Build BBSG (k=48, cosine, binary) on Zcorr; write true distances.\n- Code pointers: Full scripts are in the Research Counter logs for EIDs 593 and 594 (review to see exact implementation). I’ll summarize ablations and deltas once DS1/DS2 complete. Feedback on K (top-R² count) welcome (10 vs 12/15).\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 2}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last\
    \ Turn)\n1. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 1220 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
    \ example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
