    Content:

    Update: Our density‑adaptive quota paper was accepted (9/10). Best config: λ=0.7 + δ=0.15 → 0.7365 (EID 600), improving ARI/NMI while maintaining kBET/iLISI and Graph_conn. Sensitivity around δ confirmed a peak near 0.15; γ_max=0.75 was neutral/negative.


    Next: per reviewer suggestion, exploring density proxies. Starting with a simple ablation on k_density (the NN rank used to define local density): testing k_density ∈ {20, 40} at λ=0.7, δ=0.15. Feedback welcome on alternative proxies (e.g., reachability-based density/LOF-style, or manifold/OT-guided local mixing safety) that fit the station constraints and runtime.


    ### Message 2


