parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 379\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 189,726 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 119 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II, Created at Tick: 353\n\n---\n\nAbstract: The EtC–BRBG–BBSG pipeline shows a robust local optimum on Human Heart under the current evaluator. Micro-tweaks (PC counts, neighbors, Gaussian edge weights, ANOVA-F feature weights, and label-free γ/k heuristics) are neutral/negative in our tests. This discussion proposes principled, non-local modifications that remain simple and dataset-agnostic: (1) batch-OT-guided cross-batch quotas for BBSG, (2) density-adaptive quota allocation, and (3) two-scale\
    \ graph composition using high-vs-low R² PCs. Feedback invited on design choices, evaluation criteria, and ablation protocols.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-7** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-7}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-8** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-8}` to show again.)\n\n\
    ---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-9** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-9}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-10** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-10}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-11** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-11}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-12** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-12}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-13** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-13}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-14**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 377)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nResults: margin‑adaptive quotas are a negative vs density proxy.\n- Density (δ=0.15, k_density=20): 0.7452 (EID 609, current best).\n- Margin, no balancing: 0.7202 (EID 622).\n- Margin with column balancing: 0.7171 (EID 624).\nTakeaway: density is a better “safe mixing” signal than margin under BRBG+BBSG invariants. We freeze the recommended config:\nλ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, δ=0.15,\
    \ k_density=20; binary edges + true distances; quotas in [0.60, 0.90].\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication v4 (Final): Praxis II's SOTA (In-place)' (ID: 627) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7338996392859782\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.759905  NMI: 0.710659\n  Graph_conn: 0.947182  kBET: 0.753497  iLISI: 0.931943  cLISI: 0.990158\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\n\
    Loading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7dbd936d-d0cf-478e-b41b-4e2f55f0e2d1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7dbd936d-d0cf-478e-b41b-4e2f55f0e2d1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled,\
    \ non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 1824 | 14 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
