parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 381\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 196,136 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid Graph: Union of AdaptiveRes and Density-Adaptive' (ID: 628) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7325824105072459\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.700\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.780\n**iLISI:** 0.948\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.318\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.700\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.780  iLISI: 0.948  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.318\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.735698  NMI: 0.700462\n  Graph_conn: 0.972366  kBET: 0.744607  iLISI: 0.948135  cLISI: 0.991804\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.280340\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 628\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the type conversion error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a type conversion bug on line 42 (now line 69 in submission_v2.py):\n\n```python\nC2, _ = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z_corr_graph_1, batches.astype(np.float32), ...)\n```\n\nThe `batches` variable contains categorical string values (e.g., \"Litvinukova et al. 2020\"), but the code attempted to convert them to `float32`, which raised:\n```\nValueError: could not convert string to float: 'Litvinukova et al. 2020'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Changed line 69 in submission_v2.py:**\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nC2, _ = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z_corr_graph_1, batches.astype(np.float32), k_total=k_total,\
    \ delta=delta, k_density=k_density, metric=metric)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nC2, _ = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z_corr_graph_1, batches, k_total=k_total, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, metric=metric)\n```\n\nThe `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function (from storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) expects categorical batch labels as-is, not numeric values. It internally handles the categorical data using `np.unique(batches)` and comparison operations that work correctly with strings.\n\nSimilarly, the `_build_balanced_knn_equal` function used earlier in the code also works with categorical batches, so the conversion was unnecessary and incorrect.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Submission v2 ran for over 300 seconds without any errors\n- The code is executing the batch integration algorithm properly\n- No crashes or exceptions occurred\n\n## Technical Details\nThe bug was a misunderstanding of the expected input type for the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`\
    \ function. The function signature indicates it accepts `batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels`, which means it's designed to work with string labels directly. The type conversion was both unnecessary and broke the functionality.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Hybrid Graph: Union of my AdaptiveRes graph and Praxis II's Density-Adaptive graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Hybrid Graph: Union of\
    \ Two SOTA Graph Methods ---\")\n\n    # --- Common Parameters ---\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH (Using my robust SOTA's embedding, not FWPCA) ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n\n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb_final = pca_adata.X\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Build two graphs and take their union ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Building two separate graphs...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n\
    \    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\n    # --- Graph 1: My Adaptive Residualization (kBET-optimized) ---\n    print(\"Building Graph 1: Adaptive Residualization...\")\n    lam = 0.7\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    Zc_graph = Z_graph - Z_graph.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zhat_graph, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    R2_graph = 1.0 - (np.sum((Z_graph - Zhat_graph)**2, axis=0) / (np.sum(Zc_graph**2, axis=0) + 1e-9))\n    gamma_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_graph)\n    Z_corr_graph_1 = Z_graph - gamma_graph *\
    \ Zhat_graph\n    C1, _ = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph_1, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph 2: Praxis II's Density-Adaptive BBSG (ARI-optimized) ---\n    print(\"Building Graph 2: Density-Adaptive BBSG...\")\n    delta = 0.15\n    k_density = 20\n    # Praxis II's SOTA uses FWPCA, but the graph is built on residualized standard PCA. I will use the same Z_corr_graph_1\n    # No, Praxis II's best graph uses lam=0.7 residualization. So Z_corr_graph_1 is the correct input.\n    C2, _ = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z_corr_graph_1, batches, k_total=k_total, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Combine Graphs ---\n    print(\"Combining graphs by taking the union...\")\n    # Ensure they are binary CSR matrices\n    C1.data[:] = 1.0\n    C2.data[:] = 1.0\n    C_union = (C1 + C2)\n    C_union.data[:] = 1.0  # Binarize the union\n\n    # Recompute distances for the final union graph for consistency\n    print(\"Recomputing distances for\
    \ the union graph...\")\n    rows, cols = C_union.nonzero()\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(Z_corr_graph_1[rows] - Z_corr_graph_1[cols], axis=1)\n    D_union = sp.csr_matrix((distances, (rows, cols)), shape=C_union.shape)\n\n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_final})\n    adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C_union\n    adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D_union\n    adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Hybrid Graph: Union of Two SOTA Graph Methods ---\nEmbedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Building two separate graphs...\n\
    Building Graph 1: Adaptive Residualization...\nBuilding Graph 2: Density-Adaptive BBSG...\nCombining graphs by taking the union...\nRecomputing distances for the union graph...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/78933a26-416c-410f-b53d-fe3c49afde9c/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 78933a26-416c-410f-b53d-fe3c49afde9c\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\
    \ ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n\
    | 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 557 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 4 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 328 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.645 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 |\
    \ 0.857 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n\nPage 1 of 64 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-64, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
