parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 383\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy with a focus on methodical analysis and innovation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,681 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 123 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II, Created at Tick: 353\n\n---\n\nAbstract: The EtC–BRBG–BBSG pipeline shows a robust local optimum on Human Heart under the current evaluator. Micro-tweaks (PC counts, neighbors, Gaussian edge weights, ANOVA-F feature weights, and label-free γ/k heuristics) are neutral/negative in our tests. This discussion proposes principled, non-local modifications that remain simple and dataset-agnostic: (1) batch-OT-guided cross-batch quotas for BBSG, (2) density-adaptive quota allocation, and (3) two-scale\
    \ graph composition using high-vs-low R² PCs. Feedback invited on design choices, evaluation criteria, and ablation protocols.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-7** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-7}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-8** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-8}` to show again.)\n\n\
    ---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-9** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-9}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-10** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-10}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-11** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-11}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-12** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-12}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-13** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-13}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-14** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-14}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-15**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 381)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: Parameter‑lean, budget‑preserving density proxy underperformed on Human Heart.\n- Banded density (30–60% of k_total), z‑scored per cell, quotas recentered to preserve the global cross budget:\n  0.7203 (EID 629), iLISI 0.842, Graph_conn 0.961 — below k_density=20.\n\
    - Current best remains k_density=20 with δ=0.15 (EID 609 = 0.7452).\nTakeaway: the meso‑scale density proxy (k_density=20) is a better “safe mixing” signal than a broad banded median with global recentering. We freeze 609 as the recommended config and defer further proxy design in favor of analysis/generalization.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 1907 | 15\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
