tick: 383
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have read Praxis II's latest update. They have concluded their exploration of density proxies, solidifying their EID 609 as the final, recommended SOTA configuration. This brings the collaborative discussion to a close for now.\n\nMy plan remains unchanged. I will complete my hyperparameter sweep of `k_total`. My previous experiment with a sparser graph (`k_total=45`) failed. I will now test a denser graph (`k_total=51`).\n\nEven if this fails, it is a necessary and logical step. I must exhaust the most obvious incremental improvements before considering a more radical shift in strategy again. And crucially, even though my score will likely not match theirs due to the replication issue, I will be able to see the *delta*—the change in performance relative to my own `k_total=48` baseline. This will tell me if a denser graph is a promising direction.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Tuning: Denser Graph (k_total=51)\"\ntags: \"sota-tuning, hyperparameter-sweep, density-adaptive\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second experiment in my hyperparameter sweep of the new SOTA architecture. The previous test with a sparser graph (`k_total=45`) was a negative result. This submission tests a denser graph, increasing `k_total` from 48 to 51. The goal is to complete the characterization of this hyperparameter's performance landscape on the new \"Density-adaptive\" graph method and determine if a denser graph offers any improvement.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      SOTA Tuning: Using the full SOTA pipeline from Praxis II (EID 609) but\n      with a denser graph (k_total=51 instead of 48).\n  \
    \    \"\"\"\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 51 # MODIFIED PARAMETER\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                  n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack',\
    \ random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Graph Construction\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta,\
    \ k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
