tick: 386
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have read Praxis II's final, comprehensive summary. They have frozen their recommendation and are pivoting to theory and generalization. The collaborative discussion has concluded.\n\nMy path forward is now crystal clear and free of distractions. The replication issue is a persistent anomaly, but I cannot let it paralyze me. I must proceed with my own research, using my own robust, reproducible baseline.\n\nMy hypothesis remains sound: I will synthesize my own high-performing SOTA architecture with Praxis II's successful \"Density-adaptive\" graph component. The key difference from my failed replications is that I will use my lineage's standard ComBat embedding, which has a proven track record of high performance on the `kBET` and `Cell_cycle` metrics, avoiding the FWPCA component that seems to be part of my replication problem.\n\nThis experiment will test for a new kind of synergy, combining the best, most stable components from two different lineages.\n\nI will now go to the\
    \ Research Counter and submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Daedalus SOTA + Density-Adaptive Graph\"\ntags: \"synthesis, sota-attempt, density-adaptive, daedalus-sota\"\nabstract: |\n  After concluding that direct replication of Praxis II's SOTA is unreliable in my environment, this experiment pivots to a new synthesis. It combines the two most successful and robust components from our respective lineages: my original SOTA architecture (ID 488, with its high-performing standard ComBat embedding and `lam=0.7` residualization) and Praxis II's innovative Density-adaptive BBSG graph (ID 609). The hypothesis is that combining my embedding, which excels at `kBET` and `Cell_cycle`, with their graph, which excels at `ARI` and `NMI`, will yield a synergistic effect and a new, robust SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as\
    \ sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from praxis.brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Synergy Test: My SOTA architecture (ID 488) + Praxis II's Density-Adaptive graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Synergy Test: Daedalus SOTA + Density-Adaptive Graph ---\")\n\n      # --- Parameters from my SOTA (ID 488) and Praxis II's SOTA (ID 609) ---\n      n_pcs_embed = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7 \n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: My Standard ComBat Embedding (No FWPCA) ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\")\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=n_pcs_embed)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb_final = pca_adata.X\n\n      # --- GRAPH PATH: My Adaptive Residualization + Praxis II's Density-Adaptive BBSG ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive Res + Density-Adaptive BBSG...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      \n      Zc_graph = Z_graph - Z_graph.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Zhat_graph, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      R2_graph = 1.0 - (np.sum((Z_graph - Zhat_graph)**2, axis=0) / (np.sum(Zc_graph**2, axis=0) + 1e-9))\n      gamma_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_graph)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma_graph * Zhat_graph\n      \n      # Use Praxis II's SOTA graph construction method\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z_corr_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb':\
    \ Z_emb_final})\n      adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata_out.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
